    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168-a1">

                <pb facs="0336" n="240" xml:id="pg240"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 91.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Prince
                            Ching, etc.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-11-03"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 31.]</seg></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of the United
                    States of America, has the honor to inform your highness and your excellencies
                    of the Tsung-li Yamên that he is bringing to Peking a legation escort of 20
                    men.</p>
                <p>They will be ready to leave Tientsin very early Saturday morning, the 5th
                    instant. He therefore respectfully requests that your highness and your
                    excellencies will kindly have arranged for them such train accommodations and
                    provide such military escort as has so courteously been done for the guards
                    which his colleagues have already brought to their legations.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails himself of the occasion to assure your highness and your
                    excellencies of his highest consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
